{"ref":"BDB, גֵּרָה²","hw":"גֵּרָה²","html":"† I. <big><span dir=\"rtl\">גֵּרָה</span></big>  <strong>n.f. cud (</strong>Arabic <span dir=\"rtl\">جِرَّةٌ</span>, so called from sound of rumination?<strong>)</strong>—<span dir=\"rtl\">גֵּרָה</span> <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 11:3\" href=\"/Leviticus.11.3\">Lv 11:3</a> + 10 times—<em>cud</em>, only in legislation of clean and unclean animals, and almost always c. (<span dir=\"rtl\">ֵי</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">ַת</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">ָה</span>) <span dir=\"rtl\">מַעֲלֵה</span> <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 11:3\" href=\"/Leviticus.11.3\">Lv 11:3</a>, <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 11:4\" href=\"/Leviticus.11.4\">4</a><sup>(×2)</sup>, <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 11:5\" href=\"/Leviticus.11.5\">5</a>, <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 11:6\" href=\"/Leviticus.11.6\">6</a>, <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 11:26\" href=\"/Leviticus.11.26\">26</a> (P) <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 14:6\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.14.6\">Dt 14:6</a>, <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 14:7\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.14.7\">7</a><sup>(×2)</sup>; <span dir=\"rtl\">ג׳ יִגָּ֑ר</span> (cf. <a data-ref=\"BDB, גָּרַר\" href=\"/BDB,_גָּרַר\", dir=\"rtl\">גרר</a> Niph.) <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 11:7\" href=\"/Leviticus.11.7\">Lv 11:7</a>; <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 14:8\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.14.8\">Dt 14:8</a> has <span dir=\"rtl\">גֵּרָה</span> without vb., but read there as <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 11:7\" href=\"/Leviticus.11.7\">Lv 11:7</a> (so Sam. 𝔊 Di).","next":"BDB, גֵּרָה³","prev":"BDB, גָּרַר"}